2026-10-29T21:56:11.7045448Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7055990Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7140608Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7149219Z [0m
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7149811Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7150277Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7150473Z 
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7150725Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7151304Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7151556Z 
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7151783Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7152151Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7152352Z 
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7152959Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7153565Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7153952Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7154257Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7154635Z 
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7154845Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7155078Z 
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7155315Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7155648Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7155763Z 
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7155872Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7156013Z 
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7156371Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7156856Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7160555Z 
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7160717Z I will:
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7160851Z 
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7161052Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7161455Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7161866Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7162240Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7162516Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7162769Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7163249Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7163578Z    /root
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7181410Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7181857Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7192424Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7192944Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7193147Z 
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7196504Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7196889Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7211872Z 
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7212336Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7221225Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7221749Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7222145Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7222321Z 
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7222480Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7222680Z 
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7222909Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7223314Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7223498Z 
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7223601Z If you would like to
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7223856Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7224020Z 
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7224246Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7224708Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-10-29T21:56:11.7224882Z 
